# Ruleset: HTTP DNS
#
# Expects a reject policy.
#
# Stops mainland apps from bypassing the gateway resolver: every host here answers DNS over HTTP for an app SDK, so a client that cannot reach it falls back to the system resolver. Hang this on a policy that can be switched off rather than a hard REJECT, so a suspected false positive is tested by flipping the policy.
#
# DNSPod's public DoH under doh.pub and dns.pub is the same bypass with a general resolver behind it. The foreign public resolvers are in Proxy/DoH.list. The bare service addresses that apps dial without a name are in HttpDNSCIDR.list.
#
# A host an app needs goes in source/protected.json, and the build fails if any reject list matches it.

DOMAIN-SUFFIX,httpdns.platform.dbankcloud.cn
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,httpdns.platform.dbankcloud.com
DOMAIN,aedns.weixin.qq.com
DOMAIN,dns.jd.com
DOMAIN,dns.pub
DOMAIN,dns.wechat.com
DOMAIN,dns.weixin.qq.com
DOMAIN,dns.weixin.qq.com.cn
DOMAIN,doh.ptqy.gitv.tv
DOMAIN,doh.pub
DOMAIN,httpdns.alicdn.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.aliyuncs.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.baidu.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.baidubce.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.bilivideo.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.huaweicloud.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.meituan.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.music.163.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.music.ntes53.netease.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.n.netease.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.volcengineapi.com
DOMAIN,httpdns.yunxindns.com
DOMAIN,httpdnsmultiapi.meituan.com
DOMAIN,resolve.umeng.com
DOMAIN,resolver.mi.xiaomi.com
DOMAIN,udns.weixin.qq.com

# Alibaba's endpoint dispatch for Taobao and Alipay. Blocking it sends the apps to ordinary DNS at the cost of a slower first request; the anycast addresses they then dial stay domestic through Geo/AlibabaCIDR.list.
DOMAIN,amdc-sibling.alipay.com.cn
DOMAIN,amdc-thirdparty.alipay.com
DOMAIN,amdc.alipay.com
DOMAIN,amdc.m.taobao.com
